     <main class="page">
       <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
         <div class="eyebrow">Cat FAQ</div>
         <h1 id="faq-title">Everything you wanted to know about cats</h1>
         <p class="subtitle">
           A simple, modern FAQ with expandable answers for quick scanning and easy reading.
         </p>
       </section>

       <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
         <div class="example">
           <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
             <p class="question-text">Why do cats purr?</p>
             <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
           </button>
           <div class="details">
             Cats purr for comfort, communication, and sometimes self-soothing. It usually means
             they feel relaxed, though context matters.
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
             <p class="question-text">How much sleep do cats need?</p>
             <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
           </button>
           <div class="details">
             Most cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, and kittens or older cats may sleep
             even more.
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
             <p class="question-text">Why do cats knead blankets?</p>
             <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
           </button>
           <div class="details">
             Kneading is a comforting instinct from kittenhood. Adult cats often do it when they
             feel safe, content, or bonded with their favorite person.
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
             <p class="question-text">Do indoor cats still need enrichment?</p>
             <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
           </button>
           <div class="details">
             Yes. Scratching posts, climbing spots, puzzle feeders, and daily play help cats stay
             healthy, active, and mentally engaged.
           </div>
         </div>
       </section>
     </main>

     <script>
       document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((example) => {
         const button = example.querySelector(".question");

         button.addEventListener("click", () => {
           const open = example.classList.toggle("is-open");
           button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(open));
         });
       });
     </script>
